\par That night, as I had every night since I\rquote d left the Hudson\rquote s Estate, I dreamt of her.
\par I had always been a man subject to vibrant and very convincingly real dreams. Father Helstrom said it was proof positive that I was amongst the listless, the wanderers\'85 t
hose who could not find satisfaction in the mundanity of average life. Owing perhaps to my birth, to the father who had walked out on our family and left my mother with four pups and no coin to raise them}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f171\fs36\insrsid4213068 , chasing perhaps}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid3479529  after one of his own dreams}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid1703995 . Or}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f171\fs36\insrsid3479529 , }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid16272459 my whimsical mind could be due to}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid1703995  the i}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f171\fs36\insrsid2451557 nevitable injury}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid1703995  in a young man\rquote s heart that come
s from knowing he has been willfully orphaned. A resentment for both mother and father, and thus a weaker understanding of soc}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid5327506 ial good and the importance of my responsibility to society.}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid1703995 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid5327506 I}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid2451557  liked to think I had been diligent in pursuing instruction in under
standing social good, in being a benefit to society as a whole and not a continuing burden upon it. But I}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid5327506  did not- could not- deny that I had inherited my father\rquote 
s moral deficiencies. I was half his, after all, and had always been prone to my mind wandering, to imagination when I should have been focusing on the tasks at hand. I }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f171\fs36\insrsid5327506\charrsid5327506 
was}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid5327506  unmoored in that way. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid11211415 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid5327506 I had been working at bringing order to my mind and to my life since the Ebon Gables Abbey had taken me in as a child. Lord knows I hadn\rquote t made enough pro
gress, but I was trying. My disposition was truly one to be deplored\'85 I found myself fighting against my corrupt nature every single day, in some way.
\par But such was the curse of man. Every one of us grappled with different demons. I had to remember my struggles were not special. They were not unique. 
\par For all that I could self-correct in the waking world though, taming my mind while at rest seemed\'85 impossible. And oh}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid14947823 ,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid5327506 
 how it tortured me then.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid14947823 The dream was similar, but always just slightly different, each night I had it. It nearly always made sense in the moment, but afterwards when I woke, the pieces didn\rquote 
t fit together quite so neatly. 
\par I was in the narthex of my Abbey, the wood older, mossy around the edges, the clay tiles above the small patio cracked and
 broken, several having slid off and lying like garden stone around the entranceway. Daffodils grew up between the shattered shards and other pebbles that may have at one point formed a walkway. The door was missing entirely, welcoming me into the sunlit 
nave.
\par I stepped inside, into a kaleidoscope of color and dusty warmth. The portraits adorning the stained glass windows on either side of me shifted in every dream, sometimes Saint August looking upon me with a benevolent smile, a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 
\ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid11230260 pup}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid14947823  held in each of his burly arms}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid11230260 
. Sometimes it was the Holy Vestal Abyssinia, squash, pumpkins and gourds gathered at her feet, blooms rising in a pathway behind her. It was always one of the heroes of the scriptures that I\rquote d loved reading about growing up, }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid2451557 and}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid11230260  still loved. Always one of the Saints or Holy figures I\rquote 
d hoped were looking down on me, guiding me. Never Saint Kristoff, or Pious Charles, who }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f171\fs36\insrsid11230260\charrsid11230260 actually}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid11230260 
 adorned the nave in Ebon Gables.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \f171\fs36\insrsid14947823 
