\par The latches had stayed clasped, at least. Which was the first thing the canine woman checked}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \f187\fs32\insrsid13777146 . She knelt down }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \f187\fs32\insrsid6190639 
to place her free, trembling hand- trembling from the cold, I hoped, and not from }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \f187\fs32\insrsid13777146 the accidental fright I\rquote d given her}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \f187\fs32\insrsid6190639 
- over the closure, to make sure it was safe.
\par I began to bumble out an apology, but anything I could have said was cut off when the woman\rquote s husband turned from where }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \f187\fs32\insrsid13777146 he had}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f187\fs32\insrsid6190639  been setting the other trunk down on the drier area of cobblestone, and snarled a furious, \'93Hell\rquote s }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f187\fs32\insrsid6190639\charrsid2838023 teeth}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs32 
